(6896234, 1038980, 54446, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the blue, Christophe.  It''s a striking image.   I gave this a 5 because of the brightness of the foreground water relative to the dark stormy sky.  In the real world, bodies of water take on the nature of the sky and are always slightly darker than the sky itself.  It is perfectly okay to use artistic license to present the image in the way you wish.  However, all the bright water vs. dark sky was unnatural to my eye, since there was no direct involvement of the sun.  But, I may have lived in the mountains too long.  Also, when viewing your scene, I "heard" the water splashing on the shore or boat, rendering it less than silent.  Hope it''s okay to offer this constructive criticism.  Again, congratulations on your top score in this challenge.</td>', 'Congratulations on the blue, Christophe.  It''s a striking image.   I gave this a 5 because of the brightness of the foreground water relative to the dark stormy sky.  In the real world, bodies of water take on the nature of the sky and are always slightly darker than the sky itself.  It is perfectly okay to use artistic license to present the image in the way you wish.  However, all the bright water vs. dark sky was unnatural to my eye, since there was no direct involvement of the sun.  But, I may have lived in the mountains too long.  Also, when viewing your scene, I "heard" the water splashing on the shore or boat, rendering it less than silent.  Hope it''s okay to offer this constructive criticism.  Again, congratulations on your top score in this challenge.', '2012-11-02 08:52:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6896238, 1038994, 77196, '<td valign="top">What great wallpaper! I''m guessing circa mid- to late-1960''s.<br/> <br/>Silent testimony of the former occupant / stage in life. <br/> <br/>Looks like you tried to straighten it along the right edge, but the horizontal lines at the ceiling and floor are much more visible / noticeable. I think including a bit of floor / ceiling was required (to avoid a DQ), but straightening at the ceiling would probably have been a better choice than the right side. <br/> <br/>You''ve captured a great moment from about 50 years ago. It made me smile.</td>', 'What great wallpaper! I''m guessing circa mid- to late-1960''s. Silent testimony of the former occupant / stage in life.  Looks like you tried to straighten it along the right edge, but the horizontal lines at the ceiling and floor are much more visible / noticeable. I think including a bit of floor / ceiling was required (to avoid a DQ), but straightening at the ceiling would probably have been a better choice than the right side.  You''ve captured a great moment from about 50 years ago. It made me smile.', '2012-11-02 08:58:26.000000', NULL, 0),
