(6896295, 1038980, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dennisheckman:</b></div><hr/><i> Christophe, Congrats on winning yet again, and with a score that is below your overall average! Question for you- did you use a neutral ND filter for the horizon separation or just a standard ND filter? Or no filter at night? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks a lot Dennis. Yes, I used a ND 1000 filter. However, to get that contrasted horizon, I processed the RAW file 2 times, one time with normal exposure for the sea and fortress, and another time (lower exposure and much more contrast) for the sky. Then I blended them manually together.</td>', 'Originally posted by Dennisheckman: Christophe, Congrats on winning yet again, and with a score that is below your overall average! Question for you- did you use a neutral ND filter for the horizon separation or just a standard ND filter? Or no filter at night?   Thanks a lot Dennis. Yes, I used a ND 1000 filter. However, to get that contrasted horizon, I processed the RAW file 2 times, one time with normal exposure for the sea and fortress, and another time (lower exposure and much more contrast) for the sky. Then I blended them manually together.', '2012-11-02 10:33:13.000000', NULL, 0),
